        "body": "**Suite complete and green (2026-08-13).** Branch `nodo/cor-1257-go-nuts-embedded-real-broker-test-suite-verify-jetstream` off main@143ec67, two commits (committed, not yet pushed): `3b6f979` — the suite (`internal/brokersemantics`, **21 tests**) + `natsmsgtest` demotion + README; `f6f999f` — doc corrections from review. Both commits verified green individually (bisect-safe).\n\n**All assertion classes pass against the embedded broker:** the seven model-errors, plus normalization-vs-pedantic asserted in *both* modes (pedantic driven via raw `$JS.API` request — nats.go exposes no pedantic option), the 10116 boundary (`len > maxDeliver` rejected, `len == maxDeliver` accepted), and `backOff` with `maxDeliver -1` accepted.\n\n**Four NEW findings neither list had:**\n1. **`Ack`/`Nak`/`Term` return `nil` while the server rejects them for want of a `$JS.ACK` grant** — the COR-1224 grant-gap class is *silent at the client*. (Ticket-worthiness flagged to Andrea — this is the detection side of what E7's generated grants prevent.)\n2. `NumAckPending` is 0 on an exhausted message.\n3. Stream `ConsumerLimits` silently fill a consumer's zero fields.\n4. **The ack floor advances on stream-side message removal** — directly relevant to COR-1256's quarantine semantics (remove does un-pin the floor).\n\n**Shipping shape: the split is clean and entirely category (a)** — the suite imports only symbols on main, nothing from the A1 branch; it merges independently. Stated plainly: merging it gates the *beliefs underneath* the A1 work, not the A1 code paths themselves. Overlap with the A1 branch's `f4e160a` is two doc-only files; **suite-first merge order is cheaper** (the A1 branch then resolves mechanically — keep the suite's ConsumerLimits doc block, drop the 7-line duplicate).\n\nOpen (non-gating) decisions: where the requested-vs-stored config read-back check lives (jsconsumer at Start vs COR-1255 admission); whether findings 1/3 get their own tickets."
      },
      {
        "createdAt": "2026-08-12T16:07:45.837Z",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-12T16:07:45.795Z",
        "body": "**The assertion list, from the A1 review history + a fresh empirical probe (2026-08-12).** Seven P1 model errors — each was invisible to the `natsmsgtest` fake because it encodes the same wrong belief:\n\n1. **Term does not settle** (ENT-1492's root): floor stays pinned after Term; capture-then-Ack advances it.\n2. **Blocker identity is not derivable from `ConsumerInfo`**: `AckFloor.Stream+1` is wrong after a drain (floor jumps to the delivered high-water mark; measured floor 2, blocker at 6); `AckFloor.Consumer+1` pins to the blocker's *first* delivery and goes stale across redeliveries (measured floor 1 vs redeliveries 4, 5, 6). Assert both, on a filtered consumer, before and after a drain.\n3. **`NumDelivered` is not a ladder counter** — increments on AckWait expiry with no handler involvement (measured 4 deliveries in 68 ms).\n4. **`BackOff` does not govern Nak — it governs ack timeouts.** Measured on 3s/3s/3s: plain `Nak()` redelivers in 0 s; `NakWithDelay(3s)` in 3 s; no-ack in 3 s. This is why \"do nothing\" is the correct failure disposition under server-owned ladders.\n5. **Absent `BackOff` ≠ absent ladder** — redelivery continues on AckWait repeated.\n6. **Short `BackOff` array ≠ short ladder** — last rung repeats, counted over rungs served *before* delivery N (see COR-1255 for the off-by-one).\n7. **Non-positive `MaxDeliver` means unlimited, not invalid** — a `-1` consumer must start and consume.\n\n**Empirical corrections to the original scope (probe, 2026-08-12):**\n- `ackWait ≠ backOff[0]` is **silently normalized** by the server on the ordinary client path (AckWait 30s + BackOff [1m,2m] → stored AckWait 1m), *not* rejected. In **pedantic** JS-API mode (what NACK's controller uses) the same mismatch *is* a rejection — assert both modes, or at minimum normalization + label the pedantic case as NACK-context.\n- `len(backOff) > maxDeliver` rejected (400 / err 10116); `len == maxDeliver` **accepted** — the server's own error text (\"required to be >\") overstates its rule.\n- `backOff` alongside `maxDeliver = -1` accepted.\n\n**Build note:** no build tag — the suite runs in default `go test ./...`. A tag CI can forget is a gate that silently doesn't run. Harness partially exists (`runJetStreamServer`/`runTestEnv`, seven real-broker tests in tree); estimate is hours, not days."
      }
    ]
  },
