 	// is deliberately not a readiness condition: a remote outage already
 	// fails the publishes routed there (consumer Naks → JetStream
 	// redelivers), and gating on it would stall ALL regions' fan-out for
 	// one region's problem. Remote state is surfaced via the
 	// meta_fanout.nats.region_connected gauge + disconnect logs instead.
 	//
 	// Beyond local NATS, readiness gates on the consumer this deployment
 	// actually drives. In US/default mode that is the live webhook consumer (the
 	// backfill, PR-backfill and lifecycle consumers deliberately do NOT gate: each
 	// self-heals via its own subscribe-retry loop, so a problem on one — e.g. its
 	// stream not present yet — must not mark the pod NotReady and stall the live
 	// github_meta fan-out). In lifecycle-only mode the webhook consumer isn't
 	// started, so the lifecycle fan — the whole reason the pod runs in that region
 	// — becomes the readiness gate instead.
